# Secrets. llm.py reads the provider credential from the process environment
# first and falls back to .env; neither may ever be committed. Ship .env.example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The seeded database. NOT tracked on purpose.
#
# db.seed() rebuilds it on first import and the SEEDED DATA is reproducible:
# db.py pins random.seed(20), and a fresh seed was verified table-by-table
# against a previously shipped copy — departments, faculty, students, subjects,
# rooms, timetable, leaves, requests, exams and placements all hash identically.
#
# The FILE is not byte-identical, for two reasons worth knowing before anyone
# "fixes" this by committing it: SQLite page layout and freelist ordering are
# not reproducible, and a database that ships in git also accumulates runtime
# rows. The copy this rule replaced had five stray `audit` entries from someone
# demoing the console, committed by accident. A 244 KB binary that changes on
# every run produces unreadable diffs and merge conflicts nobody can resolve.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch
*.log
/tmp/
